(Title) Tj
T*
(Conversational AI Support for Self-Management of Atrial Fibrillation: Results from a) Tj
T*
(Randomised Trial) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(A trial randomised 480 adults with atrial fibrillation to receive either digital) Tj
T*
(conversational coaching via an interactive platform or standard clinical follow-up. The) Tj
T*
(conversational AI group received access to 24/7 dialogue-based education regarding symptom) Tj
T*
(recognition, medication adherence, and lifestyle modifications relevant to arrhythmia) Tj
T*
(management. Quality-of-life measures specific to atrial fibrillation-related limitations) Tj
T*
(were assessed at trial conclusion. Participants receiving conversational AI support) Tj
T*
(demonstrated numerically higher satisfaction with self-management resources and reported) Tj
T*
(greater confidence in recognising warning signs. User surveys indicated the interactive) Tj
T*
(platform was perceived as accessible and supportive by the majority. Engagement metrics) Tj
T*
(showed sustained interaction with the conversational system over the study period. The) Tj
T*
(usual care cohort completed standard clinic-based education and support. Quantitative) Tj
T*
(quality-of-life scores showed modest improvements in both arms, with the AI-supported) Tj
T*
(group trending toward greater gain, though formal statistical comparison revealed mixed) Tj
T*
(outcomes. This trial provides preliminary evidence that conversational AI may serve as an) Tj
T*
(acceptable adjunct to standard atrial fibrillation care delivery.) Tj
ET
